urns.response_json` column.\n- **`llm/logs.py`**:\n  - Module-level helpers: `_payload_replacements`, `condense_payload`, `resolve_payload`, `_model_json_replacements`, and `TURN_TOOLS_SQL`.\n  - `LogStore.log` stores the condensed payload on the turn.\n  - New `LogStore.turn_response_json` and `_turn_tool_pairs`.\n  - `llm logs` rows now carry the resolved `response_json`. A payload whose references no longer resolve comes back as `None` instead of failing the listing.\n- **`llm/default_plugins/openai_models.py`**: sync and async `Responses.execute` remember each reasoning done-event by item id. After `response.completed`, a new `_reasoning_refresh_events` method emits metadata events so the stored reasoning part carries the final payload's `encrypted_content`.\n\n**Checks**\n- `.venv/bin/python -m pytest -q tests/test_logs_store.py tests/test_openai_responses.py tests/test_migrate.py tests/test_llm_logs.py`: 266 passed. Before the change, 23 of these failed.\n- Full `pytest`: 998 passed.\n- `ruff check` on the three changed source files: clean.\n\n**Not verified**\n- `black` and `mypy` aren't installed in the project's `.venv`, so I couldn't run the Justfile's lint step. I ran `ruff format --check` with a `ruff` binary from another local venv. It flags the three files, but the unmodified HEAD versions are flagged too, so this predates my edits. I didn't reformat anything.\n- The spec's tests exercise only the sync streaming refresh. The async path is a mirror of it and has no test of its own.\n\n**Choices I made where the spec left room**\n- A tool name whose only long description conflicts with another is dropped. Short descriptions are skipped before the conflict check, so they don't count as \"seen\".\n- `_payload_replacements` offers `output` and `text` through the same length-and-type check as every other value.\n\nI haven't committed anything. `SPEC.md` is still untracked, as it was when I started.", "ttft_ms": 1379, "type": "result", "duration_ms": 254512, 